  "description": "Shared core of the Unified.Data.Tables storage providers: the reflection-based object-graph serializer (nested types, JSON/GZip fallback, an oversized-cell policy), the lossless large-value layout ([TableValueSplit] cells, continuation rows, blob offload behind IOffloadBlobStore), the row and request size planners, the filter translator, the type discriminators, the cache policy and the provider-neutral StorageOptions. Every provider (Azure Table Storage, in-memory, SQLite) builds on it, so they store and read exactly the same rows. Uses the Azure.Data.Tables row types, but has no network or Azure.Storage.Blobs dependency. Not meant to be referenced directly: reference a provider package.",
